{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "היענה", :translit "ha-ye'enah", :gloss "the barn owl"} {:he "שמענה את בניה", :translit "shema'enah et banehah", :gloss "it abandons its young"} {:he "ואינה מרחמת עליהם", :translit "ve-einah merachemet aleihem", :gloss "and it has no compassion on them"} {:he "העורב אכזרי על בניו", :translit "ha-orev akhzari al banav", :gloss "the raven is cruel to its young"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition of owl (v. 15) and raven (v. 14) based on shared trait of cruelty to young"}], :frame {:text "The raven's cruelty toward its offspring is noted in Leviticus 11:15 where it appears among unclean birds. The Sages describe the raven as despising its young and abandoning them, as recorded in b. Shabbat 108b and developed in Midrash Vayikra Rabbah 19:2. The owl similarly abandons its chicks without compassion, making the juxtaposition of these two species in the list of non-kosher birds in Deuteronomy 14:14–15 a meaningful textual arrangement.", :sources ["Leviticus 11:15" "b. Shabbat 108b" "Vayikra Rabbah 19:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition of owl (v. 15) and raven (v. 14) based on shared trait of cruelty to young", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:37.555595969Z", :model "glm-5.2"}